<% content_for :title, "Your data · Tastatur" %>

<div class="shell max-w-3xl">
  <div class="pt-5 rule-heavy mb-10">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold mt-5">What we hold about you</h1>
    <p class="text-ink-2 mt-3">
      No form, no identity check, no account. This page recomputes the identifier from the
      connection you are reading it on and shows you every matching row.
    </p>
  </div>

  <% if @result.nil? %>
    <div class="notice">Could not determine your connection details, so there is nothing to look up.</div>
  <% elsif @result.any? %>
    <div class="card mb-6">
      <div class="card-head">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold">
          <%= pluralize(@result.findings.size, "event") %> matching your current connection
        </h2>
        <span class="label">Last 48 hours</span>
      </div>
      <div class="max-h-[28rem] overflow-y-auto">
        <div class="bar-row label border-b border-rule sticky top-0 bg-surface">
          <span>When</span><span>Site</span><span>Page</span><span>Device</span>
        </div>
        <% @result.findings.each do |finding| %>
          <div class="bar-row">
            <span class="num text-muted shrink-0"><%= finding.occurred_at.to_fs(:short) %></span>
            <span class="bar-label"><%= finding.site_domain %></span>
            <span class="bar-label"><%= finding.path %></span>
            <span class="text-muted shrink-0">
              <%= [finding.browser, finding.os, finding.country_code].compact.join(" · ") %>
            </span>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="notice">
      This is everything. There is no name, no email, no IP address and no device identifier
      attached to any of these rows — the only thing linking them together is a digest that
      stops working when today's secret is destroyed.
    </div>
  <% else %>
    <div class="card card-body mb-6">
      <p class="font-semibold">We hold no events matching your current connection.</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 mt-3">
        If you have visited a site measured by this Tastatur instance recently, one of two things
        is true: you were not measured (Do Not Track, an ad blocker, or a site that excludes your
        network), or you were measured under a secret that has since been destroyed — which is the
        retention policy working as described.
      </p>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <section class="mt-10 space-y-6 text-[15px] leading-relaxed">
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3">Why there is no identity check</h2>
      <p>
        Verifying who you are would mean collecting more personal data than we currently hold
        about you, in order to hand back less. Instead the lookup uses your live connection: the
        address comes from the TCP session rather than from anything you could type, so this page
        cannot be pointed at anyone else. Nothing you do here is written down.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3">The formal position</h2>
      <p>
        GDPR Art.11(1) provides that where a controller is not in a position to identify a data
        subject, the rights in Arts.15–20 do not apply. That is our situation for measurement
        data. Rather than reply with only that citation, Art.11(2) invites you to supply
        information that would let us find you — loading this page is that, and the result above
        is the answer.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3">Requests about a specific site</h2>
      <p>
        The operator of the site you visited is the data controller and decides what is collected
        and for how long. Requests to erase, restrict, or object should go to them; they can
        delete a site's entire history from their dashboard at any time, which removes it here
        immediately and irreversibly.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="text-sm text-muted rule pt-6">
      <%= link_to "Full privacy documentation", privacy_path, class: "underline" %>
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
